Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:41:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: floating window tasks resize live, new
 windows and dialogs follow

A floating window task (the unfolded home) is resized by its PowOS frame.
The app keeps its buffers at the screen's size and tells the task's size
("size <id> <w> <h>"): the window is configured to it at once and drawn
at its real size from the top left as it commits - no new buffers per
step, never stretched. Configure->commit latency is logged per resize.

"export-new 1" (the app, unfolded): every new application window - one
app opening another (Dolphin -> Gwenview), a second window - opens as its
own task; turned on, the ones already on the desktop too. Dialogs and other
transients are drawn into their parent's task, where KWin placed them, and
take touch and focus. Closing such a task closes its window; one that asks
first comes back as a task with its question.
